{158}{Well, back to the Underhill farm. It's not a bad little place but it has gotten a bad reputation lately.}{Well, back to the Underhill farm. It's not a bad little place but it has gotten a bad reputation lately.}{}{}{}{}
{159}{Oh? How so?}{}{1}{}{161}{}
{160}{e:}{}{1}{}{0}{fl 190}
{161}{Well now, I'm not the type to go blathering rumors left an' right, but for the past three generations, the eldest Underhill boy has all come to a bad end! It all started with Micehel, who was the elder son of Robelo Underhill. He got it in his head to become a sailor! Imagine that. Twenty years later, one of those cross-beams came crashin' down and crushed both his feet so bad he could never walk again! Poor boy.}{Well now, I'm not the type to go blathering rumors left an' right, but for the past three generations, the eldest Underhill boy has all come to a bad end! It all started with Micehel, who was the elder son of Robelo Underhill. He got it in his head to become a sailor! Imagine that. Twenty years later, one of those cross-beams came crashin' down and crushed both his feet so bad he could never walk again! Poor boy.}{}{}{}{}
{162}{Poor boy, indeed.  What happened to him?}{}{5}{}{165}{}
{163}{Yuh, poor boy. Whut happen' to him?}{}{-4}{}{165}{}
{164}{e:}{}{1}{}{0}{fl 190}
{165}{Ol' Toby found him in Blackroot. He was strapped onto some cart with wheels, an' was scrubbin' the floors in a tavern called The Sour Barnacle. Ol' Toby brought him home and a few years later, he married one of the Chupps' girls. She had to do all the work while he stayed at home an' took care of the place. But his oldest son, Tapass, he had it even worse.}{Ol' Toby found him in Blackroot. He was strapped onto some cart with wheels, an' was scrubbin' the floors in a tavern called The Sour Barnacle. Ol' Toby brought him home and a few years later, he married one of the Chupps' girls. She had to do all the work while he stayed at home an' took care of the place. But his oldest son, Tapass, he had it even worse.}{}{}{}{}
{166}{How so?}{}{5}{}{170}{}
{167}{How?}{}{-4}{}{170}{}
{168}{e:}{}{1}{}{0}{fl 190}
{169}{}{}{}{}{}{}
{170}{After Micehel passed away, Tapass inherited the place and seemed to do alright. He got married,  - can't recall the girl's name offhand - and started a family, but he wasn't so good as a farmer. So, he finally got desperate enough that he went up north and got a job running one of those things they call a steam engine. Well, it blew up and killed him! Oh, it was terrible. Just terrible. Emily - That's her name! - was just all tore up.}{After Micehel passed away, Tapass inherited the place and seemed to do alright. He got married,  - can't recall the girl's name offhand - and started a family, but he wasn't so good as a farmer. So, he finally got desperate enough that he went up north and got a job running one of those things they call a steam engine. Well, it blew up and killed him! Oh, it was terrible. Just terrible. Emily - That's her name! - was just all tore up.}{}{}{}{}
{171}{That is terrible. For everyone. What became of her and the children?}{}{5}{}{175}{}
{172}{Oh, poor man. And poor lady! What happened to her and yung-uns?}{}{-4}{}{175}{}
{173}{e:}{}{1}{}{0}{fl 190}
{174}{}{}{}{}{}{}
{175}{She couldn't bear to live there anymore so she sold the place to Frigo and moved to Hobbiton. But her oldest boy, Tollo's his name, oh!, he grew up and became a bad'n! I heard the most awful stories about how he became a thief and was robbin' people. Last I heard about him, he was on the run down around Dernholm. So you see, that's why everyone thinks the place is no good and Frigo can't get anyone to live there.}{She couldn't bear to live there anymore so she sold the place to Frigo and moved to Hobbiton. But her oldest boy, Tollo's his name, oh!, he grew up and became a bad'n! I heard the most awful stories about how he became a thief and was robbin' people. Last I heard about him, he was on the run down around Dernholm. So you see, that's why everyone thinks the place is no good and Frigo can't get anyone to live there.}{}{}{}{}
{176}{[You start to say something about coincidences but think better of it.] I see... Well, thank you, Weqia. Now, I really must be going.}{}{5}{}{181}{}
